<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market inactive - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market inactive - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry and demand was moderate. Feedlots very current. Few available cattle priced at $70.00-$71.00, bids $69.00, last established prices were $69.00 on Thursday.</p>
<p>For the week 95,500 head confirmed including 18,900 head or about 20 percent contracted or formulated cattle. Confirmed - none</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
